From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MIRAGE <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 03:15:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] MIRAGE: render library: recorded answers for commands
 the emulator lacks

A deployment's profile carries what a real host of its kind printed for a few
commands the emulator has no class for (the text, the stream, the exit code,
the time it took). The shell asks the library before its own lookup. An entry
answers only when the emulator has no command of that name, the word typed
resolves to the entry's program and that file is still as installed, the
arguments are exactly the entry's, and the caller is one the entry answers.
Everything else is answered as before.

The gate request and the decision event gain 'tier' (emulated, rendered or
none); a rendered command is 'known'. /proc/loadavg and /proc/stat are
generated on each read from the hardware class's record, in step with the
uptime the emulator reports. With no [mirage] render_library set, nothing
changes.
